On 24 Aug 2004 rosslenbroich@itz.uni-duesseldorf.de wrote:

> i'm currently playing a quite strong wizard, unfortunately named
> "wizard". when i wanted to check something in wizmode, i used the
> usual command "nethack -D -uwizard" and stupidly saved the game. when
> i load the savefile the usual way it's still a game in wizmode. is
> there any (easy? i guess not) way to change the savefile back to a
> normal one instead of a wizmode one?

With a debugger, you should be able to manipulate the variable flags.debug
directly. Otherwise, go to  restgamestate  in restore.c and set
wizard=FALSE  after  flags  has been read, recompile, load the game and
save it to get a clean saved game.

(Disclaimer: Procedures are untested.)

